From 5db7a0ca31b31fc2c951e99e4834e00d61b52951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:19:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Added: Add desktop terminal keyboard shortcuts

Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+Shift+Tab switch tabs, Ctrl+Shift+T opens and
Ctrl+Shift+W closes a tab, Ctrl+Shift+C and Ctrl+Shift+V copy and
paste, and Ctrl+=, Ctrl+- and Ctrl+0 change the text size on the
screen. Ctrl+Shift+F and Ctrl+Shift+S are reserved for find and
snippets. The shortcuts are listed in the tab bar settings menu and can
be turned off with terminal-keyboard-shortcuts = false.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GLNsTPnn2xKUQ4uFcevT6G
